Summary: ratio analysis (key question — is K/log N bounded?)
================================================================

Max c_S/log N = 0.8643848907297586713
Min c_S/log N = 0.5901433753883364105
Max log(2 w_2)/log N = 0.24851311451025271759
Min log(2 w_2)/log N = 0.07708208977928730384
Max K/log N = 9.859260409652924950
Min K/log N = 5.634352917783484769

If max(K / log N) <= C* (a constant), then we have
    K(E) <= C* * log N(E),
hence N_0(q) <= ceil(sqrt(C* * log N(E) / h_0_thm))
 = O(sqrt(log N(E)))  (polylog in conductor).

